> So what is the proper way to get the column names of a data frame. 
> 
> RList keys() or the  "names" attribute?
> 

REXP x = /* get a data frame from somewhere */;
String s[] = x.asList().keys();


> I assume it's kosher to modify the "names vector" if I want to change the column names. Is this true?
> 

You can't really "change" anything so, no. But if you use REXPGenericVector(list) then the names attribute is set using the names of that list -- if that was your question. Technically, you can create a separate list with attributes including "names" that you pass to the REXPGenericVector(list, attr) constructor but I would not recommend that.


> It feels uncomfortable to have access to the underlying implementation. Is this going to work 5 years from now?
> 

Who knows, but I would strongly discourage assuming anything beyond the public API exactly from that reason.

Cheers,
Simon

