> out.write(r.asBytes());
> 
> I assume it's proper to modify an REXP and then still be able to send it back to R

Yes.


> and use it to create a plot, save it for later, etc. Or do I have to use R to modify a data frame e.g. c.eval('colnames(df) <- c("x", "y", "z")'); ?
> 
> For performance reasons I'd like to minimize trips back to R to do things. My app is highly interactive and it may not always be able to do everything all at once. 


Well, it really depends -- each eval and assign has to send everything across so for all practical purpose the eval to modify is faster since it doesn't need to ship all the data across again. But whether that is an issue or not depends on the size of the objects you're exchanging.

